A||N||5||Monkeyman||Replacing stock aux gauges||||5||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||10-03-2001||07:41 PM||||I'm replacing my stock aux gauges with aftermarket, electric oil pressure and volt gauges.  Can I use the stock aux gauge wiring harness?  If so, what wires should I use for what?  I won't be using the idiot lights if that makes any difference.  This is on a stock 2.8.  Do I need to run my own wiring?  If so, what do I wire and where?  I know some of you have done this before, but I can't remember who it was.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PontiacAPE.jpg">    <BR>Monkeyman||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||10-03-2001||10:51 PM||||The volt should work fine with the stock assembly, so should the oil.  As long as the oil pressure uses the same resistances that the stock one uses, 0-80 ohms, it will work off the stock harness.  Though you wont be using the idiot lights, you can still use the feed for the backlighting to light up your new gauges at night.  I can get you a diagram of the wiring if you need it, email me c311t@yahoo.com||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||10-04-2001||12:41 AM||||Thanx.  Email sent.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||10-05-2001||04:08 AM||||Email sent again.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||10-05-2001||07:35 PM||||Does anybody else know which factory wires need to be connected to the new oil pressure and volt gauges?  I have both gauges and a new sending unit (supposedly have to have that to match the oil pressure gauge).  Any help would be greatly appreciated as I'd like to wire these up and test them tomorrow.||||reg||1
